{"slug": "digital-pressure-gauge-working", "targets": ["digital pressure gauge"], "html": "<h2 style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:700;color:#0186e0;margin:34px 0 16px;\">Digital Pressure Gauge: Key Specifications to Check</h2><p>Before you buy a <strong>digital pressure gauge</strong>, compare these specifications on the data sheet. They decide whether the gauge suits field indication or calibration work.</p><div style=\"overflow-x:auto;\"><table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin:14px 0;font-size:16px;\"><tr><th style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;background:#0186e0;color:#fff;\">Specification</th><th style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;background:#0186e0;color:#fff;\">What it means</th><th style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;background:#0186e0;color:#fff;\">Typical value</th></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Accuracy</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Maximum error, usually % of full scale</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">0.05 % to 0.5 % FS</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Resolution</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Smallest digit shown</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">0.001 to 0.1 unit</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Range</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Minimum to maximum pressure</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Vacuum up to 1000 bar</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Units</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Selectable display units</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">bar, psi, kPa, MPa, kg/cm\u00b2</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Power</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Battery or loop power</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">AA cells or 4 to 20 mA</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Protection</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Housing ingress rating</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">IP65 to IP67</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Extra features</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Useful field functions</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Peak hold, tare, data logging</td></tr></table></div><p>Rule of thumb: for a test gauge, choose an accuracy at least four times better than the instrument under test, and a range where normal pressure sits in the middle half of the scale.</p>"}